{"id":"mahabharata-6-052","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":52,"title":"द्विपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 52 · Third day: the Garuda and Ardhachandra arrays","summary":{"en":"At dawn Bhishma forms the great Garuda array for the Kauravas, with Duryodhana at the back. The Pandavas answer with a crescent-shaped array and the armies close with a tremendous din.","kn":"ಉದಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಕೌರವರಿಗಾಗಿ ಗರುಡವ್ಯೂಹ ರಚಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಹಿಂಭಾಗದಲ್ಲಿರುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪಾಂಡವರು ಅರ್ಧಚಂದ್ರ ವ್ಯೂಹದಿಂದ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ಭಯಂಕರ ಘೋಷದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸಂಧಿಸುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"भोर में भीष्म कौरवों के लिए महान गरुड़ व्यूह बनाते हैं, पीछे दुर्योधन है। पाण्डव अर्धचन्द्र व्यूह से उत्तर देते हैं और सेनाएँ भारी कोलाहल के साथ भिड़ती हैं।","te":"ఉదయం భీష్ముడు కౌరవులకు గరుడ వ్యూహం పన్నుతాడు, వెనుక దుర్యోధనుడు ఉంటాడు. పాండవులు అర్ధచంద్ర వ్యూహంతో బదులిస్తారు; సేనలు భీకర ధ్వనితో తలపడతాయి.","ta":"விடியலில் பீஷ்மர் கௌரவருக்காகக் கருட வியூகம் அமைக்கிறார், பின்னால் துரியோதனன் இருக்கிறான். பாண்டவர் பிறைவடிவ வியூகத்தால் பதிலளிக்க, படைகள் பேரொலியுடன் மோதுகின்றன.","ml":"പ്രഭാതത്തിൽ ഭീഷ്മർ കൗരവർക്കുവേണ്ടി ഗരുഡ വ്യൂഹം ഒരുക്കുന്നു; പിന്നിൽ ദുര്യോധനനുണ്ട്. പാണ്ഡവർ അർധചന്ദ്രാകൃതിയിലുള്ള വ്യൂഹംകൊണ്ട് മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; ഭീകരമായ ആരവത്തോടെ സേനകൾ അടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.52; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रभातायां तु शर्वर्यां भीष्मः शांतनवस्ततः ।\nअनीकान्यनुसंयाने व्यादिदेशाथ भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When night had turned to dawn, Bhishma, son of Shantanu, gave orders to the divisions as they marched out, O Bharata."}},{"n":2,"text":"गारुडं च महाव्यूहं चक्रे शांतनवस्तदा ।\nपुत्राणां ते जयाकाङ्क्षी भीष्मः कुरुपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shantanu's son Bhishma, grandfather of the Kurus, wishing victory for your sons, made the great Garuda formation."}},{"n":3,"text":"गरुडस्य स्वयं तुण्डे पिता देवव्रतस्तव ।\nचक्षुषी च भरद्वाजः कृतवर्मा च सात्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father Devavrata himself was in Garuda's beak; Bharadvaja's son Drona and the Satvata Kritavarman were the eyes."}},{"n":4,"text":"अश्वत्थामा कृपश्चैव शीर्षमास्तां यशस्विनौ ।\nत्रिगर्तैर्मत्स्यकैकेयैर्वाटधानैश्च संयुतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthama and Kripa, both renowned, formed the head, joined by the Trigartas, Matsyas, Kekayas and Vatadhanas."}},{"n":5,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः शलः शल्यो भगदत्तश्च मारिष ।\nमद्रकाः सिन्धुसौवीरास्तथा पञ्चनदाश्च ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Shala, Shalya and Bhagadatta, sir, with the Madrakas, Sindhus, Sauviras and the people of the five rivers,"}},{"n":6,"text":"जयद्रथेन सहिता ग्रीवायां संनिवेशिताः ।\nपृष्ठे दुर्योधनो राजा सोदरैः सानुगैर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"were placed in the neck together with Jayadratha. At the back was King Duryodhana, surrounded by his brothers and followers."}},{"n":7,"text":"विन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ काम्बोजश्च शकैः सह ।\nपुच्छमासन्महाराज शूरसेनाश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two Avantis, Vinda and Anuvinda, the Kamboja with the Shakas, and all the Shurasenas formed the tail, great king."}},{"n":8,"text":"मागधाश्च कलिङ्गाश्च दाशेरकगणैः सह ।\nदक्षिणं पक्षमासाद्य स्थिता व्यूहस्य दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Magadhas and Kalingas with the hosts of Dasherakas, armored, took the right wing of the formation."}},{"n":9,"text":"काननाश्च विकुञ्जाश्च मुक्ताः पुण्ड्राविषस्तथा ।\nबृहद्बलेन सहिता वामं पक्षमुपाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kananas, Vikunjas, Muktas and Pundravishas, with Brihadbala, took the left wing."}},{"n":10,"text":"व्यूढं दृष्ट्वा तु तत्सैन्यं सव्यसाची परंतपः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नेन सहितः प्रत्यव्यूहत संयुगे ।\nअर्धचन्द्रेण व्यूहेन व्यूहं तमतिदारुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that army arrayed, the scorcher of foes Savyasachin, with Dhrishtadyumna, countered it in the battle with a crescent formation, and that formation was very fearsome."}},{"n":11,"text":"दक्षिणं शृङ्गमास्थाय भीमसेनो व्यरोचत ।\nनानाशस्त्रौघसंपन्नैर्नानादेश्यैर्नृपैर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the right horn, Bhimasena shone, surrounded by kings from many lands armed with floods of various weapons."}},{"n":12,"text":"तदन्वेव विराटश्च द्रुपदश्च महारथः ।\nतदनन्तरमेवासीन्नीलो नीलायुधैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Right after him were Virata and the great chariot-warrior Drupada, and after them Nila with his men of blue weapons."}},{"n":13,"text":"नीलादनन्तरं चैव धृष्टकेतुर्महारथः ।\nचेदिकाशिकरूषैश्च पौरवैश्चाभिसंवृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After Nila came the great chariot-warrior Dhrishtaketu, surrounded by the Chedis, Kashis, Karushas and Pauravas."}},{"n":14,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः शिखण्डी च पाञ्चालाश्च प्रभद्रकाः ।\nमध्ये सैन्यस्य महतः स्थिता युद्धाय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna and Shikhandi, the Panchalas and the Prabhadrakas stood in the middle of the great army for battle, O Bharata."}},{"n":15,"text":"तथैव धर्मराजोऽपि गजानीकेन संवृतः ।\nततस्तु सात्यकी राजन्द्रौपद्याः पञ्च चात्मजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too the king of dharma, surrounded by an elephant division; then Satyaki and the five sons of Draupadi, O king,"}},{"n":16,"text":"अभिमन्युस्ततस्तूर्णमिरावांश्च ततः परम् ।\nभैमसेनिस्ततो राजन्केकयाश्च महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"then Abhimanyu quickly, and after him Iravan, then Bhima's son Ghatotkacha, O king, and the great chariot-warrior Kekayas."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततोऽभूद्द्विपदां श्रेष्ठो वामं पार्श्वमुपाश्रितः ।\nसर्वस्य जगतो गोप्ता गोप्ता यस्य जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the best of men, Arjuna, whose protector is Janardana and who is himself protector of the whole world, took the left side."}},{"n":18,"text":"एवमेतन्महाव्यूहं प्रत्यव्यूहन्त पाण्डवाः ।\nवधार्थं तव पुत्राणां तत्पक्षं ये च संगताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the Pandavas arrayed this great formation in answer, to kill your sons and those allied with their side."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं व्यतिषक्तरथद्विपम् ।\nतावकानां परेषां च निघ्नतामितरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the battle began, with chariots and elephants entangled, as your men and the others struck one another."}},{"n":20,"text":"हयौघाश्च रथौघाश्च तत्र तत्र विशां पते ।\nसंपतन्तः स्म दृश्यन्ते निघ्नमानाः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here and there masses of horses and masses of chariots were seen charging and killing one another, lord of the people."}},{"n":21,"text":"धावतां च रथौघानां निघ्नतां च पृथक्पृथक् ।\nबभूव तुमुलः शब्दो विमिश्रो दुन्दुभिस्वनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the masses of chariots ran and struck separately, a tumultuous noise arose, mingled with the sound of drums."}},{"n":22,"text":"दिवस्पृङ्नरवीराणां निघ्नतामितरेतरम् ।\nसंप्रहारे सुतुमुले तव तेषां च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that very tumultuous clash of your side and theirs, the heroes struck one another with a noise reaching the sky, O Bharata."}}]}]}